  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'rschema_0211' comprises three tables: 'project', 'consultant', and 'service_record'.\nThe 'project' table represents a project with columns for 'Client_Name' (a string of up to 255 characters), 'End_Date' (a date and time), 'Name' (a string of up to 255 characters), 'Project_ID' (an integer, the primary key), and 'Start_Date' (a date and time).\nThe 'consultant' table represents a consultant with columns for 'Consultant_ID' (an integer, the primary key), 'Date_of_Birth' (a date and time), 'Gender' (a string of up to 255 characters), 'Name' (a string of up to 255 characters), 'Phone_Number' (a string of up to 255 characters), and 'Professional_Field' (a string of up to 255 characters).\nThe 'service_record' table represents a service record with columns for 'Consultant_ID' (an integer, not null, foreign key referencing 'consultant' table), 'Project_ID' (an integer, not null, foreign key referencing 'project' table), 'Service_Content' (a string of up to 255 characters), 'Service_Date' (a date and time), and 'Service_ID' (an integer, the primary key).\nThis schema ensures data integrity by enforcing primary keys and foreign keys, and by restricting null values in certain columns. It also allows for referential integrity by maintaining consistency between related tables.",
  "gold_question": "Consulting Service System Business Requirement Description:\nThe Technical Consulting Department provides multiple technical consulting service projects, each of which involves multiple consultants. Consulting service projects have a Project ID, Name, Start Date, End Date, and Client Name. Consultants have a Consultant ID, Name, Date of Birth, Gender, Phone Number, and Professional Field. Consulting service records need to record the Service ID, Project ID, Consultant ID, Service Date, and Service Content.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0211.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0211\nCREATE TABLE `project` (\n  `Project_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Client_Name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Start_Date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `End_Date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Project_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `consultant` (\n  `Consultant_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Date_of_Birth` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Gender` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Phone_Number` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Professional_Field` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Consultant_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `service_record` (\n  `Service_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Consultant_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Project_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Service_Content` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Service_Date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Service_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `service_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Consultant_ID`) REFERENCES `consultant` (`Consultant_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `service_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`Project_ID`) REFERENCES `project` (`Project_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
